// Was SOUNDNESS QUEUE row static_mut_write_through_borrow_admits; closed: a write into a static's storage demands 'static data (E0597).
// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row static_mut_write_through_borrow_admits (tier 2).
// NEIGHBOUR of bc_admits issue-69114-static-mut-ty, ROWED — reason 2 (doors in
// series). A write to a `static mut` is checked against its declared type with
// elided regions 'static since 2026-09-13d — at the bare write and at a place
// rooted at the static. `let p = &mut BAR; *p = &n` reaches the static's type
// through a BORROW, i.e. a READ of the static. Filling at the declaration closes
// this and refuses three legal programs (a static read meeting a local borrow in
// `pick(SR, &n)`, `eqr(SR, &n)`, `W { r: SR }.set(&n)`) through the queue row
// static_arg_pins_shared_callee_region_refused, which must open first.
// Rust: E0597 `n` does not live long enough.
package static_mut_write_through_borrow_fail;
static FOO: u8 = 4u8;
static mut BAR: &u8 = &FOO;
fn set() {
    let n: u8 = 1u8;
    unsafe {
        let p = &mut BAR;
        *p = &n;
    }
}
fn main() -> i32 { set(); unsafe { return *BAR as i32; } }
// rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024 (round 2026-09-15f-rustcaudit, class CONFIRMED): REFUSED — error[E0597]: `n` does not live long enough. Twin src/compiler/probes/2026-09-15f-rustcaudit/rust/static_mut_write_through_borrow_admits.rs. Variants: static_mut_write_through_borrow_admits__allowlint.rs REFUSED E0597. Audit note: same with #![allow(static_mut_refs)]; no lint error printed either way.
